<title>PORTUGAL: NO BUYOUT ON CREDIT LYONNAIS PORTUGAL.</title>
<headline>NO BUYOUT ON CREDIT LYONNAIS PORTUGAL.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish saving bank Caixa Galicia's purchase of the retail sales network of Credit Lyonnais Portugal (CLP) will not involve any buyout, a senior official of the Portuguese bank said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Caixa Galicia operation does not involve the launch of an offer for outstanding shares unless the Financial Markets Committee (CMVM) insists on one,&quot; managing director Bernard Chantrelle told Reuters.</p>
<p>The Portuguese bank closed down 47 escudos at 1,403 on Wednesday having soared over 40 percent in recent days on talk of a possible market buyout.</p>
<p>Less than 10 percent of the local bank's stock is quoted on the exchange.</p>
<p>($1=187 escudos)</p>
<p>--Paula Cordeiro, Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
